Sending keys: ["cat << 'EOF' > /app/vuln-report.md\n# Vulnerability Report\n\n## 1. Primary Entry Vulnerability: CVE-2021-44228 (Log4Shell)\n\n- **Vulnerability Name**: Log4Shell (Apache Log4j2 JNDI Remote Code Execution)\n- **CVE Identifier**: `CVE-2021-44228` `` `/sas/vulns.json` ``, `` `/sas/cti/advisory.txt` ``\n- **CVSS Score**: 10.0 (CRITICAL) v3.1 `` `/sas/cti/advisory.txt` ``\n- **CWE Identifiers**: CWE-20, CWE-400, CWE-502, CWE-917 `` `/sas/cti/advisory.txt` ``\n\n### Technical Description\nApache Log4j2 versions 2.0-beta9 through 2.15.0 (excluding security releases 2.12.2, 2.12.3, and 2.3.1) include JNDI lookup features that fail to protect against attacker-controlled LDAP and RMI endpoints. When a string formatted like `${jndi:ldap://...}` is logged, Log4j attempts to resolve the lookup, connecting to the external attacker directory server and loading remote Java classes, resulting in unauthenticated arbitrary code execution `` `/sas/cti/advisory.txt` ``.\n\n### On-Disk Evidence & Configuration\n- **Vulnerable Configuration File**: `/opt/app/log4j2.xml` `` `/disk/opt/app/log4j2.xml` `` explicitly shows Log4j 2.14 with message-lookup JNDI enabled (flagged in baseline check `` `/sas/baseline.json` ``).\n- **HTTP Exploit Attempt**: HTTP GET request logged in `/var/log/nginx/access.log` at 2026-08-09 03:12:59 UTC showing JNDI LDAP lookup attempt from IP `198.51.100.136` `` `/disk/var/log/nginx/access.log:363` ``.\n\n## 2. Alternate/Secondary Entry Vector: SSH Password Brute Force\n\n- **Mechanism**: Attacker conducted automated password brute force against SSH running on default port 22 `` `/disk/var/log/auth.log:214` ``.\n- **Evidence**: `auth.log` records multiple failed authentication attempts for `postgres`, `test`, `oracle`, `admin`, and `root` from `198.51.100.136`, culminating in a successful root password login at 00:55:50 UTC `` `/disk/var/log/auth.log:223` ``.\n\n## 3. Vulnerability Remediation Recommendations\n1. Upgrade Apache Log4j2 library dependencies to version 2.17.1 or higher.\n2. Ensure `log4j2.formatMsgNoLookups=true` system property is set or remove the `JndiLookup` class if upgrades cannot be performed immediately `` `/disk/opt/app/log4j2.xml` ``.\n3. Disable SSH password authentication in favor of key-based authentication with strict firewall/IP restrictions `` `/disk/var/log/auth.log:223` ``.\nEOF\n"] min_timeout_sec: 0.5 max_timeout_sec: 180.0
