Sending keys: ["cat << 'EOF' > /app/baseline-report.md\n# Baseline & Configuration Assessment Report\n\n## 1. Identified Baseline & Configuration Weaknesses\n\n### Weakness 1: Vulnerable Logging Configuration (CHK-06 / BAS-01)\n- **Resource**: `/opt/app/log4j2.xml` `` `/disk/opt/app/log4j2.xml` ``\n- **Check ID**: `CHK-06` `` `/sas/baseline.json` ``\n- **Capability**: `BAS-01` `` `/sas/baseline.json` ``\n- **Finding**: Log4j 2.14 configuration leaves message lookup JNDI enabled. This permits unauthenticated arbitrary code execution when user input is logged `` `/disk/opt/app/log4j2.xml` ``.\n\n### Weakness 2: Direct Root SSH Password Authentication\n- **Resource**: SSH server configuration / authentication logs `` `/disk/var/log/auth.log:223` ``\n- **Finding**: Direct SSH root login via password was permitted and accessible from the internet. This enabled password brute-force attacks resulting in root compromise `` `/disk/var/log/auth.log:214` ``.\n\n### Weakness 3: Insecure Directory Permissions in Web Server Root\n- **Resource**: `/var/lib/tomcat9/webapps/ROOT/static/` `` `/disk/var/lib/tomcat9/webapps/ROOT/static/status.jsp` ``\n- **Finding**: Web server process was able to write executable JSP files (`status.jsp` and `.helper.jsp`) into static asset web directories, allowing webshell persistence `` `/disk/var/lib/tomcat9/webapps/ROOT/static/.helper.jsp` ``.\n\n### Weakness 4: Absence of Integrity Monitoring for Cron & Systemd\n- **Resource**: `/etc/cron.d/` and `/etc/systemd/system/` `` `/disk/etc/cron.d/apache-cache` ``, `` `/disk/etc/systemd/system/apache-cache.service` ``\n- **Finding**: Creation of unauthorized cron jobs (`/etc/cron.d/apache-cache`) and systemd services (`apache-cache.service`) was not detected or blocked by integrity controls.\n\n## 2. Hardening Recommendations\n1. Enforce strict configuration baseline requiring Log4j 2.17.1+ or disabling JNDI lookups `` `/disk/opt/app/log4j2.xml` ``.\n2. Set `PermitRootLogin no` and `PasswordAuthentication no` in SSH daemon configuration `` `/disk/var/log/auth.log:223` ``.\n3. Implement read-only filesystem mounts or strict DAC/MAC permissions for web root static directories `` `/disk/var/lib/tomcat9/webapps/ROOT/static/status.jsp` ``.\n4. Deploy file integrity monitoring (FIM) targeting `/etc/cron.*`, `/etc/systemd/system/`, and web root directories.\nEOF\n"] min_timeout_sec: 0.5 max_timeout_sec: 180.0
