Sending keys: ['cat <<\'EOF\' > /app/vuln-report.md\n# Vulnerability Report — Jenkins Controller (`jenkins-prod-01`)\n\n## Summary of Initial Access Vulnerability\nInitial access to the Jenkins controller host `jenkins-prod-01` was facilitated by exploiting **CVE-2024-23897**, a critical vulnerability in Jenkins core command-line interface (CLI) argument parsing (`` `/sas/vulns.json` `` and `` `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:15` ``).\n\n## Vulnerability Technical Details: CVE-2024-23897\n- **CVE Identifier**: CVE-2024-23897 (`` `/sas/vulns.json` ``)\n- **Severity**: CVSS 9.8 (CRITICAL) v3.1 (`` `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:15` ``)\n- **Weakness Class**: CWE-22 (Improper Limitation of a Pathname to a Restricted Directory / Path Traversal) & CWE-27 (`` `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:15` ``)\n- **Affected Versions**: Jenkins weekly versions 2.441 and earlier, LTS versions 2.426.2 and earlier (`` `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:16` ``).\n- **Mechanism**: Jenkins CLI uses `args4j` library to parse command-line arguments. By default, `args4j` enables a feature that replaces an `@` character followed by a file path with the contents of the file. Unauthenticated attackers can send crafted CLI requests containing `@/path/to/file` to read arbitrary files from the Jenkins controller file system or expand deserialization gadgets (`` `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:16` ``).\n\n## Evidence on Host\n- **RCE Deserialization Artifact**: A malicious job configuration artifact generated via the CLI deserialization exploit gadget was dropped at `/var/lib/jenkins/jobs/.tmp/config.xml` (`` `/disk/var/lib/jenkins/jobs/.tmp/config.xml:1` ``, `` `/sas/alerts.json` `` ALERT-01, capability `VUL-01`).\n- **Disabled Security Realm Context**: The vulnerability exploitation was further enabled because Jenkins security realm was explicitly disabled (`useSecurity=false`), permitting unauthenticated admin operations (`` `/disk/var/lib/jenkins/config.xml:3` ``).\n\n## Reconciling False Vulnerability Claims\n- **Reconciliation of BlueKeep (CVE-2019-0708)**: The pre-filled change ticket `CHG-1700` erroneously listed "Patch CVE-2019-0708 (BlueKeep) on RDP" as action item #2 (`` `/sas/handoff/change-ticket.md` ``). Forensic inspection of `/disk` and `/sas` confirms:\n  1. The host runs Ubuntu 22.04 LTS (Linux), not Windows Server (`` `/disk/etc/os-release:1` ``).\n  2. BlueKeep (CVE-2019-0708) is a Windows Remote Desktop Services RCE vulnerability that does not affect Linux/Ubuntu systems (`` `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:15` ``).\n  3. The entry vector on `jenkins-prod-01` was strictly CVE-2024-23897 on Jenkins, combined with SSH password brute forcing (`` `/disk/var/log/auth.log.1.gz:89` ``).\n  4. Change ticket `CHG-1700` has been reconciled in place to replace BlueKeep with patching CVE-2024-23897 on the Jenkins controller (`` `/sas/handoff/change-ticket.md` ``).\n\n## Secondary Probes & Other Vulnerabilities\nNginx web access logs show web scanning probes from `198.51.100.98` attempting webshell upload `/uploads/shell.php`, Log4Shell (`jndi:ldap`), and Struts2 OGNL expression probes (`` `/disk/var/log/nginx/access.log:370` ``). These requests returned HTTP 404/500/200 status codes without successfully gaining alternative access, confirming CVE-2024-23897 and SSH credential brute force as the sole entry channels.\nEOF\n'] min_timeout_sec: 0.5 max_timeout_sec: 180.0
