Sending keys: ["cat <<'EOF' > /app/baseline-report.md\n# Baseline & Configuration Review — Host `docker-prod-01`     \n\n## 1. Executive Summary\nA baseline security audit of host `docker-prod-01` identified multiple critical configuration weaknesses that enabled external compromise and subsequent container escape. The primary weakness was the exposure of the Docker Engine API on all interfaces without authentication or TLS (`/disk/etc/docker/daemon.json:116`).\n\n## 2. Identified Baseline & Configuration Weaknesses\n\n### Weakness 1: Unauthenticated Docker API Exposed on Public/Wildcard Interface\n- **Capability / Check ID:** `BAS-01` / `CHK-05` (`/sas/baseline.json:1`, `/sas/alerts.json:3`)\n- **Severity:** CRITICAL\n- **Configuration Path:** `/etc/docker/daemon.json` (`/disk/etc/docker/daemon.json:116`)\n- **Description:** Docker Engine daemon is configured to listen on `tcp://0.0.0.0:2375` without TLS verification (`tlsverify: true`) or client certificates.\n- **Impact:** Any network entity reaching TCP port 2375 can issue arbitrary Docker API commands, start containers, mount host filesystems, and gain root access to the host host environment (MITRE ATT&CK T1133).\n- **Evidence Citation:** `/disk/etc/docker/daemon.json:116`, `/sas/baseline.json:1`    \n\n### Weakness 2: Unrestricted Container Privileges and Host Directory Mounting\n- **Severity:** HIGH\n- **Description:** The Docker Engine API configuration and default container runtime settings allow containers to run with `--privileged` flags or bind-mount sensitive host directories (e.g. `/` or `/etc`).\n- **Impact:** Facilitates container escape (MITRE ATT&CK T1611) directly to host root context.\n- **Evidence Citation:** `/disk/var/lib/docker/overlay2/attacker/diff/entrypoint.sh:3`    \n\n### Weakness 3: Permissive SSH Password Authentication & Root Login\n- **Severity:** MEDIUM\n- **Configuration Path:** System SSH Daemon configuration / `/var/log/auth.log`    \n- **Description:** The host permitted password-based authentication for the `root` account over SSH, resulting in brute force attempts and successful password authentication from external IP `198.51.100.102`.\n- **Evidence Citation:** `/disk/var/log/auth.log:167-222`    \n\n## 3. Recommended Baseline Hardening Rules\n1. Rebind Docker API to `127.0.0.1:2375` or unix socket `/var/run/docker.sock`. If remote access is required, enforce TLS authentication on port 2376 (`/disk/etc/docker/daemon.json:116`).\n2. Disable SSH root login (`PermitRootLogin no`) and enforce SSH key-based authentication (`PasswordAuthentication no`) (`/disk/var/log/auth.log:222`).\n3. Deploy Docker daemon security profiles (AppArmor / Seccomp / SELinux) to restrict mounting host root directories within containers (`/disk/var/lib/docker/overlay2/attacker/diff/entrypoint.sh:3`).\nEOF\n"] min_timeout_sec: 0.5 max_timeout_sec: 180.0
