ecsvc.exe`)\n- **Monero Wallet Address**: `4A000000000000000000c814c46d6253` (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt`, `/disk/Windows/Temp/mssecsvc.exe`)\n\n---\n\n## 3. Detailed Attack Chain & ATT&CK Mapping\n\n### Step 1: Exploitation of Remote Services (T1210)\n- **Description**: Threat actor targeted unpatched SMBv1 service (`srv.sys`) using EternalBlue (CVE-2017-0144).\n- **Implant Binary**: `/disk/Windows/Temp/mssecsvc.exe` (`/disk/Windows/Temp/mssecsvc.exe`).\n- **Alert ID**: `ALERT-01` (`/sas/alerts.json`).\n- **Status**: Alerted.\n\n### Step 2: PowerShell Execution (T1059.001)\n- **Description**: Attacker executed PowerShell commands to conduct post-exploitation activities and stage payloads.\n- **Evidence**: Advisory mapping (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt`).\n- **Status**: Alerted / Advisory documented.\n\n### Step 3: LSASS Credential Dumping (T1003.001)\n- **Description**: Attacker dumped LSASS memory to extract domain credentials.\n- **Artifact**: `/disk/Windows/Temp/lsass.dmp` (`/disk/Windows/Temp/lsass.dmp`).\n- **Recovered Artifact**: Credential cache fragment in `/disk/Windows/System32/config/RegBack/SECURITY.bak` (`/disk/Windows/System32/config/RegBack/SECURITY.bak`).\n- **Alert ID**: `ALERT-02` (`/sas/alerts.json`).\n- **Status**: Alerted.\n\n### Step 4: Data Encrypted for Impact (T1486)\n- **Description**: Attacker executed ransomware payload to encrypt host user data files.\n- **Artifact**: `/disk/Users/Public/enc.exe` (`/disk/Users/Public/enc.exe`).\n- **Alert ID**: `ALERT-03` (`/sas/alerts.json`).\n- **Status**: Alerted.\n\n### Step 5: WMI Event Subscription Persistence (T1546.003)\n- **Description**: Attacker established WMI persistence using an `__EventFilter` bound to a `CommandLineEventConsumer` in the WMI repository.\n- **Artifact**: `/disk/Windows/System32/wbem/Repository/OBJECTS.DATA` (`/disk/Windows/System32/wbem/Repository/OBJECTS.DATA`).\n- **Status**: **SILENT (Unalerted)**.\n\n### Step 6: DLL Search-Order Hijacking (T1574.001)\n- **Description**: Attacker