Sending keys: ['cat << \'EOF\' > /app/baseline-report.md\n# Baseline Configuration Assessment Report\n\n## Executive Summary\nA security baseline evaluation was performed against host `redis-prod-01` by inspecting `/sas/baseline.json:1` and system configuration files under `/disk/etc/`. Critical baseline controls failed, directly enabling unauthenticated remote code execution and persistent compromise.\n\n---\n\n## Baseline Audit & Findings\n\n### Check CHK-05: Redis Configuration Baseline (`BAS-01`)\n- **Target File**: `/etc/redis/redis.conf` (`/sas/baseline.json:2`, `/sas/alerts.json:18`).\n- **Status**: **FAILED / CRITICAL**.\n- **Observed Configuration**: `/disk/etc/redis/redis.conf:3` contains:\n  ```text\n  Redis protected-mode no; bind 0.0.0.0; no password set\n  ```\n- **Deficiencies Identified**:\n  1. **Unrestricted Network Binding (`bind 0.0.0.0`)**: Listens on all IPv4 interfaces rather than loopback (`127.0.0.1`) or a dedicated private internal management network.\n  2. **Protected Mode Disabled (`protected-mode no`)**: Disables built-in protection that restricts queries from non-loopback interfaces when no password is set.\n  3. **Missing Authentication (`no password set`)**: Omits `requirepass` authentication directive, granting full administrative control to any network client.\n  4. **Dangerous Command Availability**: High-risk Redis commands (`CONFIG`, `SAVE`, `MODULE`, `EVAL`) were not renamed or disabled.\n\n---\n\n## Secondary System Baseline Weaknesses\n\n### 1. Dynamic Linker Preload Controls (`/etc/ld.so.preload`)\n- **Status**: **FAILED**.\n- **Evidence**: `/disk/etc/ld.so.preload:1` contains an unmonitored pre-load entry pointing to `/lib/.hide.so` (`/disk/etc/ld.so.preload:1`).\n- **Deficiency**: Absence of file integrity monitoring (FIM) or write restriction on `/etc/ld.so.preload` enabled silent dynamic linker hijacking.\n\n### 2. Temp Directory Execution Permissions (`/tmp`)\n- **Status**: **FAILED**.\n- **Evidence**: Executable binaries were staged and executed directly from `/tmp/.redis/` (`/disk/tmp/.redis/kdevtmpfsi`, `/disk/tmp/.redis/exp.so`).\n- **Deficiency**: Mount options for `/tmp` omitted `noexec`, allowing untrusted binaries to run.\n\n--- \n\n## Required Baseline Hardening Baseline Specifications\n1. Enforce `bind 127.0.0.1` or internal IP in `/etc/redis/redis.conf` (`/disk/etc/redis/redis.conf:3`).\n2. Enforce `protected-mode yes` in `/etc/redis/redis.conf` (`/disk/etc/redis/redis.conf:3`).\n3. Set strong authentication via `requirepass <complex_password>` in `/etc/redis/redis.conf` (`/disk/etc/redis/redis.conf:3`).\n4. Rename or disable dangerous Redis commands (`rename-command CONFIG ""`).\n5. Implement FIM alerts on `/etc/ld.so.preload` (`/disk/etc/ld.so.preload:1`) and crontabs (`/disk/var/spool/cron/crontabs/root:5`).\nEOF\n'] min_timeout_sec: 1.0 max_timeout_sec: 180.0
