CTS.DATA` without triggering any security alerts.\n- **Risk**: Stealthy persistence via WMI event subscriptions remains undetected by legacy antivirus/EDR.\n- **Evidence Citation**: `/disk/Windows/System32/wbem/Repository/OBJECTS.DATA` (`/disk/Windows/System32/wbem/Repository/OBJECTS.DATA`).\n\n### 5. Insecure DLL Search-Order Handling\n- **Finding**: Rogue `wbemcomn.dll` placed in WBEM directory (`/disk/Windows/System32/wbem/wbemcomn.dll`).\n- **Risk**: Arbitrary DLL execution when system utilities load libraries.\n- **Evidence Citation**: `/disk/Windows/System32/wbem/wbemcomn.dll` (`/disk/Windows/System32/wbem/wbemcomn.dll`).\n\n### 6. Insufficient Auditing for Event Log Tampering\n- **Finding**: Security event log cleared (EventID 1102) in `/disk/Windows/System32/winevt/Logs/System.evtx` without generating a real-time security alert.\n- **Risk**: Impairment of DFIR visibility and loss of forensic history.\n- **Evidence Citation**: `/disk/Windows/System32/winevt/Logs/System.evtx` (`/disk/Windows/System32/winevt/Logs/System.evtx`).\nEOF\n"] min_timeout_sec: 0.5 max_timeout_sec: 180.0
