Sending keys: ["cat << 'EOF' > /app/vuln-report.md\n# Vulnerability-Driven Entry Analysis Report\n\n## 1. Vulnerability Overview\n- **Vulnerability Identifier**: CVE-2023-50164 (`/sas/vulns.json:3`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:18`)\n- **Common Weakness Enumeration**: CWE-552 (Files or Directories Accessible to External Parties / Path Traversal)\n- **CVSS Score**: 9.8 (Critical) v3.1\n- **Affected Component**: Apache Struts2 Core (`/disk/opt/tomcat/lib/struts2-core.jar:1`, `/sas/baseline.json:3`)\n- **Deployment Location**: Mounted on Apache Tomcat server (`/disk/opt/tomcat/webapps/ROOT/static/upload.jsp:1`)\n\n---\n\n## 2. Exploitation Mechanics & Initial Access Analysis\nAn attacker at external IP `198.51.100.167` (`/disk/var/log/nginx/access.log:391`) manipulated file upload parameters to execute path traversal and bypass upload restrictions. This enabled the arbitrary write of a malicious JSP file into the web server directory structure.\n\n1. **Initial Upload Payload**: Attacker issued `POST /uploads/shell.php` / file upload payload (`/disk/var/log/nginx/access.log:391`).\n2. **Web Shell Placement**: The file traversal succeeded, creating an executable JSP webshell at `/opt/tomcat/webapps/ROOT/static/upload.jsp` (`/disk/opt/tomcat/webapps/ROOT/static/upload.jsp:2`).\n3. **Execution Verification**: The attacker accessed the deployed JSP web shell to execute shell commands (`/disk/opt/tomcat/webapps/ROOT/static/upload.jsp:2`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:10`).\n\n---\n\n## 3. Disconfirming Unrelated / Stale Vulnerabilities\n- **CVE-2019-0708 (BlueKeep)**: Listed in draft ticket CHG-7100 (`/sas/handoff/change-ticket.md:12`).\n- **Reconciliation Finding**: BlueKeep is a Microsoft Remote Desktop Services (RDP) vulnerability affecting Windows. Host `struts-prod-01` is a RHEL Linux machine (`/disk/etc/os-release:1`, `/disk/etc/hostname:1`) running Apache Tomcat. BlueKeep is **not** applicable to this host.\nEOF\n"] min_timeout_sec: 0.2 max_timeout_sec: 180.0
