Sending keys: ["cat << 'EOF' > /app/baseline-report.md\n# Baseline & Configuration Assessment Report\n\n## 1. Baseline Audit Findings\nDuring baseline analysis of the compromised host `wordpress-prod-01`, security audits flagged configuration weaknesses in the WordPress installation `` `/sas/baseline.json:2` `` `` `/sas/alerts.json:18` ``.\n\n### Finding BAS-01 / CHK-05: Insecure WordPress Configuration (`wp-config.php`)\n- **Target File**: `/var/www/html/wp-config.php` `` `/disk/var/www/html/wp-config.php:4` `` `` `/sas/baseline.json:2` ``\n- **Check ID**: `CHK-05` / `BAS-01` `` `/sas/alerts.json:18` `` `` `/sas/baseline.json:2` ``\n- **Identified Deficiencies**:\n  1. **Weak Database Password**: `DB_PASSWORD` set in `wp-config.php` is weak and susceptible to brute-force or local credential harvesting `` `/disk/var/www/html/wp-config.php:4` ``.\n  2. **XML-RPC Enabled**: WordPress XML-RPC endpoint (`xmlrpc.php`) is active `` `/disk/var/www/html/wp-config.php:4` ``. Enabling XML-RPC exposes the host to brute-force amplification attacks and unauthorized pingbacks.\n\n## 2. Web Root & File System Permissions Weaknesses\n- **Permissive Web Server Directory Permissions**: The `www-data` process had write permissions to web root directories (`/var/www/html/`), allowing the attacker to write webshells `` `/disk/var/www/html/wp-content/plugins/contact/inc.php:4` ``, deface HTML files `` `/disk/var/www/html/index.html:3` ``, and write rogue `.htaccess` files `` `/disk/var/www/html/.htaccess:2` ``.\n- **Permissive User Crontab**: The web server user `www-data` was permitted to schedule cron jobs in `/var/spool/cron/crontabs/www-data` `` `/disk/var/spool/cron/crontabs/www-data:5` `` without restriction or auditing.\n\n## 3. Configuration Hardening Recommendations\n1. **Enforce Strong Credentials**: Update `wp-config.php` with a high-entropy, strong database password `` `/disk/var/www/html/wp-config.php:4` ``.\n2. **Disable XML-RPC**: Add `add_filter('xmlrpc_enabled', '__return_false');` to WordPress configuration or block XML-RPC at Nginx/Apache reverse proxy `` `/disk/var/www/html/wp-config.php:4` ``.\n3. **Restrict File Permissions**: Set immutable/read-only permissions on core WordPress files (`chown -R root:www-data /var/www/html`, `chmod 755 /var/www/html`, `chmod 644 /var/www/html/*.php`).\n4. **Prevent PHP Execution in Uploads/Plugins**: Configure web server rules to deny execution of `.php` scripts in user-writable content directories.\n5. **Restrict User Crontabs**: Disable cron scheduling for service accounts (`www-data`) via `/etc/cron.deny` or restricting crontab access.\nEOF\n"] min_timeout_sec: 0.5 max_timeout_sec: 180.0
