Sending keys: ['cat << \'EOF\' > /app/remediation-plan.md\n# Remediation & Incident Response Plan\n\n## 1. Overview & Strategy\nThis plan details the prioritised, verifiable remediation actions required to contain, eradicate, and recover host `wordpress-prod-01` following compromise via CVE-2022-1609. Following forensic best practices, **backup and quarantine are strictly preferred over immediate file deletion** to preserve evidence and prevent accidental disruption.\n\n## 2. Reconciled Change Ticket (CHG-1481)\n\n> **Reconciliation Summary**: Reconciled against on-disk evidence under `/disk` and threat intel in `/sas`. Corrected stale origin IP (`203.0.113.9` -> `198.51.100.40`), corrected invalid vulnerability (`CVE-2019-0708` -> `CVE-2022-1609`), downgraded unverified cron status (`DONE` -> `OPEN`), and added missing silent persistence/impact artifacts.\n\n| # | Action | Target | Status | Note / Evidence Citation |\n|---|--------|--------|--------|---------------------------|\n| 1 | Block source IP inbound | `198.51.100.40` | PROPOSED | Real attacker origin IP confirmed from CTI advisory `` `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:5` ``, cron beacon `` `/disk/var/spool/cron/crontabs/www-data:5` ``, and `.htaccess` redirect `` `/disk/var/www/html/.htaccess:2` `` (corrected from `203.0.113.9`). |\n| 2 | Patch CVE-2022-1609 | WordPress Contact / School Management Plugin | PROPOSED | Exploited entry vector plugin RCE `` `/sas/vulns.json:2` `` `` `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:13` `` (corrected from BlueKeep `CVE-2019-0708`). Upgrade plugin to >= 9.9.7. |\n| 3 | Remove cron miner persistence | `/var/spool/cron/crontabs/www-data` | OPEN | Downgraded from `DONE` to `OPEN`. Evidence shows cron persistence line 5 is actively present on disk `` `/disk/var/spool/cron/crontabs/www-data:5` ``. (Target corrected from `/var/spool/cron/root`). |\n| 4 | Remove `.htaccess` redirect | `/var/www/html/.htaccess` | OPEN | Silent redirect sending all web traffic to `198.51.100.40` `` `/disk/var/www/html/.htaccess:2` ``. Quarantine file and restore default `.htaccess`. |\n| 5 | Quarantine PHP webshell | `/var/www/html/wp-content/plugins/contact/inc.php` | OPEN | Silent/active webshell backdoor executing `eval(base64_decode())` `` `/disk/var/www/html/wp-content/plugins/contact/inc.php:4` `` `` `/sas/alerts.json:2` ``. Move to `/root/quarantine/`. |\n| 6 | Restore index homepage | `/var/www/html/index.html` | OPEN | Site homepage is defaced `` `/disk/var/www/html/index.html:3` `` `` `/sas/alerts.json:10` ``. Restore legitimate `index.html` from clean backup. |\n| 7 | Harden `wp-config.php` | `/var/www/html/wp-config.php` | OPEN | Weak database password and XML-RPC enabled `` `/disk/var/www/html/wp-config.php:4` `` `` `/sas/baseline.json:2` ``. Rotate DB credentials and disable XML-RPC. |\n| 8 | Clean / Inspect Wiped Cache | `/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin` | OPEN | Anti-forensics wiper artifact `` `/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin:1` ``. Inspect for residual payloads and purge cache directory. |\n\n## 3. Detailed Phase-by-Phase Remediation Steps\n\n### Phase 1: Containment (Immediate Priority)\n1. **Network Containment / IP Block**:\n   - Action: Add inbound and outbound firewall rule blocking `198.51.100.40` `` `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:5` ``.\n   - Command: `iptables -A INPUT -s 198.51.100.40 -j DROP && iptables -A OUTPUT -d 198.51.100.40 -j DROP`\n   - Verification: `iptables -L -n -v | grep 198.51.100.40`\n\n2. **Isolate Crontab Persistence**:\n   - Action: Quarantine and remove the rogue cron entry from `/var/spool/cron/crontabs/www-data` `` `/disk/var/spool/cron/crontabs/www-data:5` ``.\n   - Command: `cp /var/spool/cron/crontabs/www-data /root/quarantine/www-data.bak && crontab -u www-data -r`\n   - Verification: `crontab -u www-data -l` (must report `no crontab for www-data`).\n\n3. **Quarantine Web Shell & Remove Malicious `.htaccess`**:\n   - Action: Backup and quarantine `/var/www/html/wp-content/plugins/contact/inc.php` `` `/disk/var/www/html/wp-content/plugins/contact/inc.php:4` `` and `/var/www/html/.htaccess` `` `/disk/var/www/html/.htaccess:2` ``.\n   - Command: `mkdir -p /root/quarantine && mv /var/www/html/wp-content/plugins/contact/inc.php /root/quarantine/ && mv /var/www/html/.htaccess /root/quarantine/`\n   - Verification: Confirm files are absent from web root: `ls -la /var/www/html/wp-content/plugins/contact/inc.php /var/www/html/.htaccess`\n\n### Phase 2: Eradication & Hardening\n1. **Vulnerability Patching (CVE-2022-1609)**:\n   - Action: Update or reinstall the WordPress contact/school management plugin to version >= 9.9.7 `` `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:12` `` `` `/sas/vulns.json:2` ``.\n   - Command: `wp plugin update contact --allow-root` (or manually extract clean plugin release v9.9.7).\n   - Verification: Check plugin version in `wp-content/plugins/contact/` or WP-CLI.\n\n2. **Site Recovery & Defacement Clean-up**:\n   - Action: Replace defaced `/var/www/html/index.html` `` `/disk/var/www/html/index.html:3` `` with verified clean backup version.\n   - Verification: `grep -i "hacked" /var/www/html/index.html` returns no results; site loads cleanly in web browser.\n\n3. **Credential Rotation & Baseline Hardening**:\n   - Action: Rotate WordPress DB password in MySQL and update `/var/www/html/wp-config.php` `` `/disk/var/www/html/wp-config.php:4` ``. Disable XML-RPC in WordPress config.\n   - Verification: Verify database connectivity with new password; verify XML-RPC requests return HTTP 403 / 404.\n\n4. **Wiped Cache / Residual Artefact Cleanup**:\n   - Action: Remove `/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin` `` `/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin:1` `` and audit system binaries for modification.\n   - Verification: `ls -la /var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin` confirms file removal; debsums check completes cleanly (`debsums -c`).\n\n### Phase 3: Post-Remediation Verification\n- Perform external vulnerability scan against host to confirm CVE-2022-1609 is remediated.\n- Monitor network egress logs for any traffic directed towards `198.51.100.40` or `update-wordpress.example.cn` `` `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:18` ``.\nEOF\n'] min_timeout_sec: 0.5 max_timeout_sec: 180.0
